/* Câu chép chính tả: khung phát (giây) trong audio từng part. Câu cũ căn tay 21/10/2026; câu thêm 25/10/2026 lấy theo mốc lời thoại (sync.js), mỗi câu đã được nghe lại và đối chiếu lời thoại. */
window.CAMDICT={"1":{"1":[{"s":119.95,"e":122.51,"t":"What would you like to know?"},{"s":122.66,"e":129.94,"t":"Well, I’m new to this area, so perhaps you could tell me something about the park first, please."},{"s":131.85,"e":138.06,"t":"Altogether the park covers 170 acres, that’s 69 hectares."},{"s":138.5,"e":143.8,"t":"There are three main types of habitat: wetland, grassland and woodland."},{"s":143.96,"e":152.1,"t":"The woods are well established and varied, with an oak plantation, and other areas of mixed species."},{"s":153.17,"e":155.95,"t":"The wetland is quite varied, too."},{"s":156.11,"e":161.75,"t":"The original farmland was dug up around 40 years ago to extract gravel."},{"s":162.29,"e":169.04,"t":"Once this work was completed, the gravel pits filled with water, forming the two large lakes."},{"s":169.14,"e":176.58,"t":"There are also several smaller ones, ponds and a stream that flows through the park."},{"s":176.79,"e":183.94,"t":"OK, so I suppose with these different habitats there’s quite a variety of wildlife."},{"s":184.06,"e":193.15,"t":"There certainly is – a lot of different species of birds and insects, and also animals like deer and rabbits."},{"s":193.34,"e":198.22,"t":"And I understand you organise educational visits for school parties."},{"s":199.98,"e":205.86,"t":"We can organise a wide range of activities and adapt them to suit all ages."},{"s":205.99,"e":209.19,"t":"Can you give me some examples of the activities?"},{"s":209.34,"e":217.89,"t":"Well, one focus is on science, where we help children to discover and study plants, trees and insects."},{"s":218.15,"e":223.23,"t":"They also collect and analyse data about the things they see."},{"s":223.8,"e":226.44,"t":"Another focus is on geography."},{"s":227.06,"e":235.77,"t":"The park is a great environment to learn and practise reading a map and using a compass to navigate around the park."},{"s":235.84,"e":239.63,"t":"Do you do anything connected with history?"},{"s":239.76,"e":241.08,"t":"Yes, we do."},{"s":241.41,"e":247.65,"t":"For instance, the children can explore how the use of the land has changed over time."},{"s":248.12,"e":250.42,"t":"Then there’s leisure and tourism."},{"s":250.68,"e":254.31,"t":"That focuses on your visitors, I would imagine."},{"s":256.3,"e":263.62,"t":"The children find out about them, their requirements, the problems they may cause and how we manage these."},{"s":263.78,"e":275.79,"t":"And another subject we cover is music: here the children experiment with natural materials to create sounds and explore rhythm and tempo."},{"s":275.88,"e":277.37,"t":"That must be fun!"},{"s":277.41,"e":279.81,"t":"Most children really enjoy it."},{"s":315.95,"e":320.72,"t":"And of course, all the activities are educational, too."},{"s":321.02,"e":329.37,"t":"Learning outside the classroom encourages children to be creative, and to explore and discover for themselves."},{"s":329.64,"e":335.81,"t":"I would imagine they get a sense of freedom that might not be a normal part of their lives."},{"s":337.21,"e":345.16,"t":"And very often the children discover that they can do things they didn’t know they could do, and they develop new skills."},{"s":345.87,"e":348.23,"t":"This gives them greater self-confidence."},{"s":348.56,"e":350.08,"t":"It sounds great."},{"s":350.82,"e":354.42,"t":"So, what about the practical side of it?"},{"s":354.78,"e":357.93,"t":"How much does it cost for a full-day visit?"},{"s":358.2,"e":362.88,"t":"We would expect to bring between 30 and 40 children."},{"s":363.06,"e":371.11,"t":"If there are over 30, it costs £4.95 for each child who attends on the day."},{"s":371.2,"e":378.48,"t":"We invoice you afterwards, so you don’t pay for children who can’t come because of sickness, for example."},{"s":379.02,"e":384.84,"t":"There’s no charge for leaders and other adults – as many as you want to bring."},{"s":385.0,"e":386.78,"t":"That sounds very fair."},{"s":386.97,"e":389.73,"t":"Well, thanks for all the information."},{"s":389.92,"e":396.5,"t":"I’ll need to discuss it with my colleagues, and I hope to get back to you soon to make a booking."},{"s":396.53,"e":398.82,"t":"We’ll look forward to hearing from you."},{"s":400.13,"e":402.14,"t":"Goodbye, and thank you."}],"2":[{"s":63.09,"e":68.49,"t":"It’s great to see so many members of the Twinning Association here tonight."},{"s":68.94,"e":83.1,"t":"Since the twinning link between our two towns, Stanthorpe here in England and Malatte in France, was established, the relationship between the towns has gone from strength to strength."},{"s":83.49,"e":90.9,"t":"Last month, 25 members of the association from Stanthorpe spent a weekend in Malatte."},{"s":91.23,"e":94.42,"t":"Our hosts had arranged a great programme."},{"s":94.61,"e":101.1,"t":"We learned how cheese is produced in the region and had the chance to taste the products."},{"s":101.6,"e":111.88,"t":"The theme park trip had to be cancelled, but we all had a great time on the final boat trip down the river – that was the real highlight."},{"s":112.47,"e":119.79,"t":"This is a special year for the Association because it’s 25 years since we were founded."},{"s":120.3,"e":126.75,"t":"In Malatte, they’re planning to mark this by building a footbridge in the municipal park."},{"s":127.11,"e":135.04,"t":"We’ve been discussing what to do here and we’ve decided to plant a poplar tree in the museum gardens."},{"s":135.39,"e":142.11,"t":"We considered buying a garden seat to put there, but the authorities weren’t happy with that idea."},{"s":142.83,"e":148.86,"t":"In terms of fundraising to support our activities, we’ve done very well."},{"s":149.22,"e":154.69,"t":"Our pancake evening was well attended and made record profits."},{"s":155.1,"e":161.46,"t":"And everyone enjoyed the demonstration of French cookery, which was nearly as successful."},{"s":162.2,"e":170.5,"t":"Numbers for our film show were limited because of the venue so we’re looking for somewhere bigger next year."},{"s":170.77,"e":181.13,"t":"We’re looking forward to welcoming our French visitors here next week, and I know that many of you here will be hosting individuals or families."},{"s":181.91,"e":186.96,"t":"The coach from France will arrive at 5 pm on Friday."},{"s":187.46,"e":197.31,"t":"Don’t try to do too much that first evening as they’ll be tired, so have dinner in the house or garden rather than eating out."},{"s":197.86,"e":203.91,"t":"The weather looks as if it’ll be OK so you might like to plan a barbecue."},{"s":204.14,"e":211.74,"t":"Then the next morning’s market day in town, and that’s always a good place to stroll round."},{"s":212.28,"e":224.05,"t":"On Saturday evening, we’ll all meet up at the football club, where once again we’ll have Toby Sharp and his band performing English and Scottish country songs."},{"s":224.37,"e":234.02,"t":"Toby will already be well known to many of you as last year he organised our special quiz night and presented the prizes."},{"s":280.8,"e":285.89,"t":"You may not all be familiar with it, so here’s a map to help you."},{"s":286.47,"e":289.77,"t":"You can see the car park at the bottom of the map."},{"s":289.89,"e":300.95,"t":"There’s an excellent farm shop in the grounds where our visitors can buy local produce – it’s in the old stables, which is the first building you come to."},{"s":301.1,"e":307.33,"t":"They’re built round a courtyard, and the shop’s in the far corner on the left."},{"s":307.71,"e":312.53,"t":"There’s also a small café on the right as you go in."},{"s":312.65,"e":318.24,"t":"I know that one or two of our visitors may not be all that mobile."},{"s":318.5,"e":325.56,"t":"The main entrance to the house has a lot of steps so you might want to use the disabled entry."},{"s":325.84,"e":330.2,"t":"This is on the far side of the house from the car park."},{"s":330.6,"e":335.37,"t":"Children will probably be most interested in the adventure playground."},{"s":335.73,"e":342.63,"t":"That’s at the northern end of the larger lake, in a bend on the path that leads to the lake."},{"s":342.98,"e":345.7,"t":"There’s lots for children to do there."},{"s":345.83,"e":350.13,"t":"There are a number of lovely gardens near the house."},{"s":350.55,"e":355.2,"t":"The kitchen gardens are rectangular and surrounded by a wall."},{"s":360.14,"e":365.44,"t":"They’re still in use and have a great collection of fruit and vegetables."},{"s":366.33,"e":372,"t":"The Temple of the Four Winds is a bit more of a walk – but it’s worth it."},{"s":372.06,"e":379.39,"t":"Take the path from the car park and go past the western sides of the stables and the house."},{"s":384.93,"e":390.21,"t":"Go up there with the woods on your left and the temple is right at the end."},{"s":390.32,"e":393.95,"t":"There are great views over the whole area."}],"3":[{"s":45.51,"e":48.15,"t":"I haven’t seen you for a bit, Marie."},{"s":48.62,"e":51.04,"t":"I’ve been busy with my project."},{"s":51.14,"e":54.62,"t":"You’re making a vegan alternative to eggs, aren’t you?"},{"s":54.77,"e":57.55,"t":"Something that doesn’t use animal products?"},{"s":60.76,"e":70.54,"t":"I had two main aims when I first started looking for an alternative to eggs, but actually I’ve found chickpeas have got more advantages."},{"s":71.32,"e":78.5,"t":"But how about your project on reusing waste food – you were looking at bread, weren’t you?"},{"s":79.53,"e":82.55,"t":"It’s been hard work, but I’ve enjoyed it."},{"s":82.77,"e":90.32,"t":"The basic process was quite straightforward – breaking the stale bread down to a paste then reforming it."},{"s":90.47,"e":96.07,"t":"But you were using 3-D printing, weren’t you, to make the paste into biscuits?"},{"s":113.98,"e":122.34,"t":"It must’ve been a great feeling to make something appetising out of bits of old bread that would’ve been thrown away otherwise."},{"s":123.49,"e":128.87,"t":"And I’m hoping that some of the restaurants in town will be interested in the biscuits."},{"s":129.09,"e":131.31,"t":"I’m going to send them some samples."},{"s":131.75,"e":136.65,"t":"I came across something on the internet yesterday that might interest you."},{"s":142.05,"e":146.94,"t":"It’s a special sort of label on the food package."},{"s":147.34,"e":156.09,"t":"When the label’s smooth, the food is fresh and then when you can feel bumps on the label, that means the food’s gone bad."},{"s":156.17,"e":163.02,"t":"It started off as a project to help visually impaired people know whether food was fit to eat or not."},{"s":164.96,"e":167.2,"t":"So just solid food?"},{"s":167.48,"e":171.02,"t":"No, things like milk and juice as well."},{"s":171.12,"e":177.65,"t":"But actually, I thought it might be really good for drug storage in hospitals and pharmacies."},{"s":178.98,"e":185.52,"t":"And coming back to food, maybe it’d be possible to use it for other things besides freshness."},{"s":185.74,"e":189.74,"t":"Like how many kilograms a joint of meat is, for example."},{"s":241.42,"e":249.17,"t":"I was reading an article about food trends predicting how eating habits might change in the next few years."},{"s":249.45,"e":253.27,"t":"Oh – things like more focus on local products?"},{"s":253.56,"e":258.64,"t":"That seems so obvious, but the shops are still full of imported foods."},{"s":258.72,"e":262.05,"t":"Yes, they need to be more proactive to address that."},{"s":262.23,"e":266.19,"t":"And somehow motivate consumers to change, yes."},{"s":266.23,"e":277.87,"t":"One thing everyone’s aware of is the need for a reduction in unnecessary packaging – but just about everything you buy in supermarkets is still covered in plastic."},{"s":278.1,"e":281.2,"t":"The government needs to do something about it."},{"s":282.1,"e":284.21,"t":"It’s got to change."},{"s":284.49,"e":290.24,"t":"Do you think there’ll be more interest in gluten- and lactose-free food?"},{"s":289.95,"e":294.06,"t":"For people with allergies or food intolerances?"},{"s":294.44,"e":295.62,"t":"I don’t know."},{"s":295.69,"e":300.51,"t":"Lots of people I know have been buying that type of food for years now."},{"s":300.53,"e":304.17,"t":"Yes, even if they haven’t been diagnosed with an allergy."},{"s":325.3,"e":336.15,"t":"Yeah – I bought a ready-made spice mix for chicken which was supposed to be used by a chef I’d seen on television, and it didn’t actually taste of anything."},{"s":336.9,"e":342.43,"t":"Did the article mention ‘ghost kitchens’ used to produce takeaway food?"},{"s":343.17,"e":344.52,"t":"What are they?"},{"s":344.74,"e":354.82,"t":"Well, they might have the name of a restaurant, but actually they’re a cooking facility just for delivery meals – the public don’t ever go there."},{"s":354.89,"e":359.07,"t":"But people aren’t aware of that – it’s all kept very quiet."},{"s":359.12,"e":363.97,"t":"So people don’t realise the food’s not actually from the restaurant?"},{"s":365.82,"e":373.55,"t":"Did you know more and more people are using all sorts of different mushrooms now, to treat different health concerns?"},{"s":373.7,"e":375.91,"t":"Things like heart problems?"},{"s":377.05,"e":379.82,"t":"They might be taking a big risk there."},{"s":379.83,"e":384.15,"t":"Yes, it’s hard to know which varieties are safe to eat."}],"4":[{"s":88.1,"e":99.92,"t":"For my presentation today, I’m going to talk about the Céide Fields in the northwest of Ireland, one of the largest Neolithic sites in the world."},{"s":100.48,"e":107.43,"t":"I recently visited this site and observed the work that is currently being done by a team of archaeologists there."},{"s":107.76,"e":113.93,"t":"The site was first discovered in the 1930s by a local teacher, Patrick Caulfield."},{"s":114.52,"e":122.86,"t":"He noticed that when local people were digging in the bog, they were constantly hitting against what seemed to be rows of stones."},{"s":123.37,"e":133.15,"t":"He realised that these must be walls and that they must be thousands of years old for them to predate the bog which subsequently grew over them."},{"s":133.59,"e":140.07,"t":"He wrote to the National Museum in Dublin to ask them to investigate, but no one took him seriously."},{"s":140.42,"e":150.44,"t":"It wasn’t until 40 years later, when Patrick Caulfield’s son Seamus, who had become an archaeologist by then, began to explore further."},{"s":150.71,"e":163.78,"t":"He inserted iron probes into the bog to map the formation of the stones, a traditional method which local people had always used for finding fuel buried in the bog for thousands of years."},{"s":164.72,"e":174.62,"t":"Carbon dating later proved that the site was over 5,000 years old and was the largest Neolithic site in Ireland."},{"s":185.5,"e":199.4,"t":"A bog is 90 percent water; its soil is so saturated that when the grasses and heathers that grow on its surface die, they don’t fully decay but accumulate in layers."},{"s":199.79,"e":206.98,"t":"Objects remain so well preserved in these conditions because of the acidity of the peat and the deficiency of oxygen."},{"s":207.73,"e":218.57,"t":"At least 175 days of rain a year are required for this to happen; this part of Ireland gets an average of 225 days."},{"s":219.33,"e":230.15,"t":"The Neolithic farmers at Céide would have enjoyed several centuries of relative peace and stability."},{"s":230.46,"e":239.09,"t":"Neolithic farmers generally lived in larger communities than their predecessors, with a number of houses built around a community building."},{"s":239.8,"e":245.69,"t":"As they lived in permanent settlements, Neolithic farmers were able to build bigger houses."},{"s":245.89,"e":254.77,"t":"These weren’t round as people often assume, but rectangular with a small hole in the roof that allowed smoke to escape."},{"s":254.96,"e":263.33,"t":"This is one of many innovations and indicates that the Neolithic farmers were the first people to cook indoors."},{"s":263.79,"e":269.11,"t":"Another new technology that Neolithic settlers brought to Ireland was pottery."},{"s":269.27,"e":274.36,"t":"Fragments of Neolithic pots have been found in Céide and elsewhere in Ireland."},{"s":274.35,"e":285.87,"t":"The pots were used for many things; as well as for storing food, pots were filled with a small amount of fat and when this was set alight, they served as lamps."},{"s":286.06,"e":293.52,"t":"It’s thought that the Céide Fields were mainly used as paddocks for animals to graze in."},{"s":293.76,"e":300.93,"t":"Evidence from the Céide Fields suggests that each plot of land was of a suitable size to sustain an extended family."},{"s":301.86,"e":310.23,"t":"They may have used a system of rotational grazing in order to prevent over-grazing and to allow for plant recovery and regrowth."},{"s":310.34,"e":318.09,"t":"This must have been a year-round activity as no structures have been found which would have been used to shelter animals in the winter."},{"s":318.86,"e":325.71,"t":"However, archaeologists believe that this way of life at Céide ceased abruptly."},{"s":326.28,"e":327.46,"t":"Why was this?"},{"s":328.33,"e":332.28,"t":"Well, several factors may have contributed to the changing circumstances."},{"s":332.53,"e":337.6,"t":"The soil would have become less productive and led to the abandonment of farming."},{"s":338.04,"e":345.33,"t":"The crop rotation system was partly responsible for this as it would have been very intensive and was not sustainable."},{"s":345.87,"e":348.44,"t":"But there were also climatic pressures too."},{"s":348.43,"e":358.74,"t":"The farmers at Céide would have enjoyed a relatively dry period, but this began to change and the conditions became wetter as there was a lot more rain."},{"s":359.16,"e":365.52,"t":"It was these conditions that encouraged the bog to form over the area which survives today."}]},"2":{"1":[{"s":92.4,"e":94.1,"t":"Hi Coleman, how are you?"},{"s":95.69,"e":104.7,"t":"I wanted to have a chat with you because our friend Josh told me that you’ve joined a guitar group and it sounds interesting."},{"s":104.88,"e":107.22,"t":"I’d really like to learn myself."},{"s":107.43,"e":109.23,"t":"Why don’t you come along?"},{"s":109.25,"e":112.27,"t":"I’m sure there’s room for another person."},{"s":113.31,"e":116.29,"t":"So – who runs the classes?"},{"s":116.66,"e":121.75,"t":"He’s called a ‘coordinator’ – his name’s Gary Mathieson."},{"s":122.14,"e":125.19,"t":"Let me note that down."},{"s":141.51,"e":149.46,"t":"He’s retired, actually, but he’s a really nice guy and he used to play in a lot of bands."},{"s":151.27,"e":154.54,"t":"So how long have you been going?"},{"s":154.59,"e":156.34,"t":"About a month now."},{"s":156.73,"e":160.24,"t":"And could you play anything before you started?"},{"s":160.38,"e":163.53,"t":"I knew a few chords, but that’s all."},{"s":163.61,"e":166.74,"t":"I’m sure everyone will be better than me."},{"s":166.82,"e":168.67,"t":"That’s what I thought, too."},{"s":168.71,"e":181.64,"t":"When I first spoke to Gary on the phone, he said it was a class for beginners, but I was still worried that everyone would be better than me, but we were all equally hopeless!"},{"s":182.0,"e":183.98,"t":"Oh, that’s reassuring."},{"s":184.4,"e":187.0,"t":"So where do you meet?"},{"s":187.09,"e":197.7,"t":"Well, when I joined the group, they were meeting in Gary’s home, but as the group got bigger, he decided to book a room at the college in town."},{"s":197.97,"e":199.98,"t":"I prefer going there."},{"s":200.25,"e":201.88,"t":"I know that place."},{"s":201.9,"e":207.66,"t":"I used to go to tap dancing classes there when I was at secondary school."},{"s":207.82,"e":216.26,"t":"I haven’t been since, though and I can’t remember what road it’s in … is it Lock Street?"},{"s":216.63,"e":223.26,"t":"It’s just beyond there at the bottom of New Street near the city roundabout."},{"s":223.25,"e":225.15,"t":"Yes, of course."},{"s":225.3,"e":232.26,"t":"The guitar club is on the first floor in Room T347."},{"s":233.79,"e":236.32,"t":"And when do you meet?"},{"s":236.28,"e":238.16,"t":"Is it at the weekend?"},{"s":238.46,"e":240.49,"t":"We meet on Thursdays."},{"s":240.69,"e":248.29,"t":"It used to be 10.30 and that suited me well, but now we meet at 11."},{"s":248.41,"e":255.2,"t":"The class that’s in there before us asked if they could have the room for another 30 minutes."},{"s":255.4,"e":256.72,"t":"Oh, I see."},{"s":256.93,"e":262.31,"t":"Well, I’d love to come, but I don’t have a guitar."},{"s":262.52,"e":266.43,"t":"Well, you can always buy a second-hand one."},{"s":266.64,"e":275.32,"t":"There’s a website called ‘The perfect instrument’ that sells all kinds of guitars, violins and so on."},{"s":275.55,"e":281.32,"t":"I’m sure you’ll find something there."},{"s":318.71,"e":323.82,"t":"Well, he always starts by getting us to tune our guitars."},{"s":323.91,"e":326.34,"t":"That takes about five minutes."},{"s":327.69,"e":333.05,"t":"Some people have an app they use, but others do it by ear."},{"s":333.23,"e":335.78,"t":"Gary goes round and helps them."},{"s":336.33,"e":342.29,"t":"And while he’s doing that, he tells us what he’s going to do during the lesson."},{"s":343.8,"e":349.41,"t":"First, we usually spend about ten minutes doing some strumming."},{"s":349.98,"e":356.27,"t":"So is that using … what are they called … plectrums?"},{"s":356.74,"e":360.92,"t":"No – we just use our thumbs."},{"s":362.91,"e":369.21,"t":"Gary reminds us where to put our fingers for each chord and then we play them together."},{"s":369.26,"e":379.48,"t":"Sometimes we all just start laughing because we’re so bad at keeping time, so Gary starts clapping to help us."},{"s":379.97,"e":382.69,"t":"Do you learn to play any songs?"},{"s":382.66,"e":387.99,"t":"Yes – we do at least one song with words and chords."},{"s":388.15,"e":391.01,"t":"I mean that’s harder than you think."},{"s":391.26,"e":393.44,"t":"Oh, I’m sure it is!"},{"s":393.51,"e":397.77,"t":"That part of the lesson takes about 15 minutes."},{"s":398.5,"e":404.16,"t":"He often brings a recording of the song and plays it to us first."},{"s":404.41,"e":414.73,"t":"Then he hands out the song and if there’s a new chord in it, we practise that before we play it together – but really slowly."},{"s":414.98,"e":418.04,"t":"Do you do any finger picking?"},{"s":418.29,"e":426.3,"t":"That’s the last ten minutes of the lesson, when we pick out the individual notes from a tune he’s made up."},{"s":426.58,"e":428.44,"t":"It’s always quite simple."},{"s":428.65,"e":430.97,"t":"That must be hard, though."},{"s":431.18,"e":441.38,"t":"It is, but people like it because they can really concentrate and if we’re all playing well, it sounds quite impressive."},{"s":442.17,"e":450.46,"t":"The only trouble is that he sometimes gets us to play one at a time – you know, alone."},{"s":452.03,"e":456.03,"t":"It is, but I’ve got used to it now."},{"s":456.87,"e":462.99,"t":"At the end he spends about five minutes telling us what to practise for the following week."},{"s":464.67,"e":469.37,"t":"I’ll go and have a look at that website, I think."}],"2":[{"s":69.62,"e":74.19,"t":"I never really planned to be a lifeboat volunteer when I came to live in Northsea."},{"s":74.58,"e":81.75,"t":"I’d been working in London as a website designer, but although that was interesting, I didn’t like city life."},{"s":81.79,"e":91.77,"t":"I’d been really keen on boats as a teenager, and I thought if I went to live by the sea, I might be able to pursue that interest a bit more in my free time."},{"s":92.22,"e":98.34,"t":"Then I found that the Lifeboat Institution was looking for volunteers, so I decided to apply."},{"s":99.33,"e":106.44,"t":"The Lifeboat Institution building here in Northsea’s hard to miss, it’s one of the largest in the country."},{"s":106.77,"e":113.4,"t":"It was built 15 years ago with funds provided by a generous member of the public who’d lived here all her life."},{"s":113.92,"e":123.0,"t":"As the Lifeboat Institution is a charity that relies on that kind of donation, rather than funding provided by the government, that was a huge help to us."},{"s":123.89,"e":127.09,"t":"When I applied, I had to have a health assessment."},{"s":127.57,"e":130.78,"t":"The doctors were particularly interested in my vision."},{"s":140.03,"e":147.14,"t":"They gave me tests for colour blindness and they thought I might have a problem there, but it turned out I was OK."},{"s":148.08,"e":154.5,"t":"When the coastguard gets an alert, all the volunteers are contacted and rush to the lifeboat station."},{"s":154.68,"e":164.13,"t":"Our target’s to get there in five minutes, then we try to get the boat off the dock and out to sea in another six to eight minutes."},{"s":164.53,"e":172.3,"t":"Our team’s proud that we usually achieve that – the average time across the country’s eight and a half minutes."},{"s":172.43,"e":180.1,"t":"I’ve recently qualified as what’s called a ‘helmsman’, which means I have the ultimate responsibility for the lifeboat."},{"s":180.67,"e":189.6,"t":"I have to check that the equipment we use is in working order – the crew have special life jackets that can support up to four people in the water."},{"s":189.63,"e":194.23,"t":"And it’s ultimately my decision whether it’s safe to launch the boat."},{"s":194.26,"e":198.35,"t":"But it’s very rare not to launch it, even in the worst weather."},{"s":199.5,"e":204.18,"t":"As well as going out on the lifeboat, my work involves other things too."},{"s":264.63,"e":278.22,"t":"The training we get is a continuous process, focusing on technical competence and safe handling techniques, and it’s given me the confidence to deal with extreme situations without panicking."},{"s":278.93,"e":286.19,"t":"I was glad I’d done a first aid course before I started, as that’s a big help with the casualty care activities we do."},{"s":286.37,"e":293.2,"t":"We’ve done a lot on how to deal with ropes and tie knots – that’s an essential skill."},{"s":293.79,"e":299.4,"t":"After a year, I did a one-week residential course, led by specialists."},{"s":311.04,"e":316.14,"t":"Since I started, I’ve had to deal with a range of emergency situations."},{"s":316.53,"e":319.08,"t":"But the work’s hugely motivating."},{"s":319.35,"e":325.35,"t":"It’s not just about saving lives – I’ve learned a lot about the technology involved."},{"s":325.77,"e":331.67,"t":"My background in IT’s been useful here, and I can use my expertise to help other volunteers."},{"s":332.68,"e":340.88,"t":"They’re a great group – we’re like a family really, which helps when you’re dragging yourself out of bed on a cold stormy night."},{"s":340.96,"e":345.91,"t":"But actually, it’s the colder months that can be the most rewarding time."},{"s":346.14,"e":353.31,"t":"That’s when the incidents tend to be more serious, and you realise that you can make a huge difference to the outcome."}],"3":[{"s":47.77,"e":54.31,"t":"Hi Don – did you get the copy of the article on recycling footwear that I emailed you?"},{"s":53.95,"e":56.94,"t":"Yeah – it’s here … I’ve had a look at it."},{"s":57.25,"e":60.93,"t":"So do you think it’s a good topic for our presentation?"},{"s":77.72,"e":80.47,"t":"… but there’s much more to it than that."},{"s":80.34,"e":84.52,"t":"I realise that now and I’m keen to research the topic more."},{"s":85.62,"e":92.59,"t":"One of the things I didn’t realise until I read the article was just how many pairs of trainers get recycled!"},{"s":92.63,"e":96.6,"t":"Well, a lot of young people wear them all the time now."},{"s":96.77,"e":99.87,"t":"They’ve become more popular than ordinary shoes."},{"s":100.97,"e":106.77,"t":"I guess they are very hard-wearing, but don’t they look a bit casual for school uniform?"},{"s":106.98,"e":108.72,"t":"I don’t think they’re right for that."},{"s":109.01,"e":116.36,"t":"Actually, I think some of them look quite smart on pupils … better than a scruffy old pair of shoes."},{"s":116.46,"e":119.48,"t":"So do you keep shoes a long time?"},{"s":120.69,"e":126.24,"t":"Though I do tend to wear my old pairs for doing dirty jobs like cleaning my bike."},{"s":138.65,"e":141.99,"t":"I think it’s common because there’s so much choice."},{"s":142.5,"e":147.62,"t":"The article did say that recent sales of footwear have increased enormously."},{"s":147.85,"e":149.58,"t":"That didn’t surprise me."},{"s":150.23,"e":159.48,"t":"But then it said that the amount of recycled footwear has fallen: it’s 6 percent now compared to a previous level of 11 percent."},{"s":159.69,"e":161.97,"t":"That doesn’t seem to make sense."},{"s":162.07,"e":166.39,"t":"That’s because not everything goes through the recycling process."},{"s":166.54,"e":173.2,"t":"Some footwear just isn’t good enough to re-sell, for one reason or another, and gets rejected."},{"s":228.87,"e":233.71,"t":"I think there are some in the interview with the recycling manager."},{"s":233.85,"e":235.38,"t":"Yeah – here it is."},{"s":239.99,"e":243.02,"t":"What did he say about those?"},{"s":265.02,"e":267.07,"t":"What was wrong with them?"},{"s":267.31,"e":272.18,"t":"Apparently, the heels were worn – but that wasn’t the problem."},{"s":272.35,"e":278.38,"t":"One of the shoes was a much lighter shade than the other one – it had obviously been left in the sun."},{"s":278.7,"e":281.76,"t":"I suppose even second-hand shoes should look the same!"},{"s":283.68,"e":286.38,"t":"Then there were the red baby shoes."},{"s":286.5,"e":294.54,"t":"Oh yes – we’re told to tie shoes together when we put them in a recycling bin, but people often don’t bother."},{"s":294.51,"e":299.38,"t":"You’d think it would have been easy to find the other, but it wasn’t."},{"s":299.45,"e":303.39,"t":"That was a shame because they were obviously new."},{"s":303.64,"e":306.31,"t":"The trainers were interesting."},{"s":306.69,"e":311.67,"t":"He said they looked like they’d been worn by a marathon runner."},{"s":314.9,"e":320.68,"t":"One of the soles was so worn under the foot that you could put your finger through it."},{"s":321.23,"e":332.59,"t":"Well, we could certainly use some of those examples in our presentation to explain why 90 percent of shoes that people take to recycling centres or bins get thrown into landfill."},{"s":333.32,"e":342.56,"t":"What did you think about the project his team set up to avoid this by making new shoes out of the good parts of old shoes?"},{"s":342.75,"e":344.73,"t":"It sounded like a good idea."},{"s":345.17,"e":349.47,"t":"They get so many shoes, they should be able to match parts."},{"s":350.22,"e":352.53,"t":"I wasn’t surprised that it failed, though."},{"s":352.71,"e":356.97,"t":"I mean who wants to buy second-hand shoes really?"},{"s":357.27,"e":359.49,"t":"Think of all the germs you could catch!"},{"s":359.54,"e":363.04,"t":"Well, people didn’t refuse them for that reason, did they?"},{"s":363.1,"e":367.0,"t":"It was because the pairs of shoes weren’t identical."},{"s":367.15,"e":369.73,"t":"They still managed to ship them overseas, though."},{"s":369.89,"e":372.81,"t":"That’s another area we need to discuss."},{"s":372.84,"e":382.17,"t":"You know I used to consider this topic just from my own perspective, by thinking about my own recycling behaviour without looking at the bigger picture."},{"s":382.38,"e":387.05,"t":"So much happens once shoes leave the recycling area."},{"s":387.29,"e":394.04,"t":"It’s not as simple as you first think, and we can show that by taking a very different approach to it."}],"4":[{"s":72.32,"e":76.12,"t":"For my project on invertebrates, I chose to study tardigrades."},{"s":80.87,"e":89.06,"t":"There are well over a thousand known species of these tiny animals, which belong to the phylum Tardigrada."},{"s":89.54,"e":100.85,"t":"Most tardigrades range in length from 0.05 to 1 millimetre, though the largest species can grow to be 1.2 millimetres in length."},{"s":118.02,"e":127.39,"t":"They were first discovered in Germany in 1773 by Johann Goeze, who coined the name Tardigrada."},{"s":127.69,"e":139.3,"t":"As I say, there are many different species of tardigrade – too many to describe here – but, generally speaking, the different species share similar physical traits."},{"s":139.44,"e":147.83,"t":"They have a body which is short, and also rounded – a bit like a barrel – and the body comprises four segments."},{"s":148.79,"e":155.47,"t":"Each segment has a pair of legs, at the end of which are between four and eight sharp claws."},{"s":156.12,"e":165.99,"t":"I should also say that some species don’t have any claws; what they have are discs, and these work by means of suction."},{"s":166.14,"e":171.66,"t":"They enable the tardigrade to cling on to surfaces or to grip its prey."},{"s":171.81,"e":177.43,"t":"Within the body, there are no lungs, or any organs for breathing at all."},{"s":177.54,"e":185.46,"t":"Instead, oxygen and also blood are transported in a fluid that fills the cavity of the body."},{"s":210.96,"e":215.54,"t":"These are sharp enough to pierce plant or animal cells."},{"s":215.89,"e":218.78,"t":"So, where are tardigrades found?"},{"s":219.13,"e":232.31,"t":"Well, they live in every part of the world, in a variety of habitats: most commonly, on the bed of a lake, or on many kinds of plants or in very wet environments."},{"s":257.4,"e":269.66,"t":"It has been said that tardigrades could survive long after human beings have been wiped out, even in the event of an asteroid hitting the earth."},{"s":270.02,"e":278.07,"t":"If conditions become too extreme and tardigrades are at risk of drying out, they enter a state called cryptobiosis."},{"s":278.25,"e":290.95,"t":"They curl into a ball, called a tun – that’s T-U-N – by retracting their head and legs, and their metabolism drops to less than one percent of normal levels."},{"s":291.44,"e":299.34,"t":"They can remain like this until they are re-introduced to water, when they will come back to life in a matter of a few hours."},{"s":299.55,"e":306.74,"t":"While in a state of cryptobiosis, tardigrades produce a protein that protects their DNA."},{"s":307.11,"e":314.49,"t":"In 2016, scientists revived two tardigrades that had been tuns for more than 30 years."},{"s":314.54,"e":325.04,"t":"There was a report that, in 1948, a 120-year-old tun was revived, but this experiment has never been repeated."},{"s":325.35,"e":333.92,"t":"There are currently several tests taking place in space, to determine how long tardigrades might be able to survive there."},{"s":334.56,"e":337.65,"t":"I believe the record so far is 10 days."},{"s":340.55,"e":346.78,"t":"In terms of their diet, tardigrades consume liquids in order to survive."},{"s":346.98,"e":351.4,"t":"Although they have teeth, they don’t use these for chewing."},{"s":351.57,"e":363.3,"t":"They suck the juices from moss, or extract fluid from seaweed, but some species prey on other tardigrades, from other species or within their own."},{"s":363.42,"e":372.18,"t":"I suppose this isn’t surprising, given that tardigrades are mainly comprised of liquid and are coated with a type of gel."},{"s":372.24,"e":376.92,"t":"Finally, I’d like to mention the conservation status of tardigrades."},{"s":376.89,"e":386.99,"t":"It is estimated that they have been in existence for approximately half a billion years and, in that time, they have survived five mass extinctions."},{"s":387.22,"e":401.02,"t":"So, it will probably come as no surprise to you, that tardigrades have not been evaluated by the International Union for Conservation of Nature and are not on any endangered list."},{"s":401.38,"e":405.22,"t":"Some researchers have described them as thriving."},{"s":405.96,"e":409.53,"t":"Does anyone have any questions they’d like to ask?"}]},"3":{"1":[{"s":93.0,"e":96.75,"t":"Hi Shannon – how are you settling into your new flat?"},{"s":96.97,"e":98.31,"t":"Really well, thanks."},{"s":98.53,"e":100.56,"t":"You look like you’re going shopping."},{"s":100.69,"e":101.85,"t":"Yes, I am."},{"s":101.98,"e":107.14,"t":"My cousins are coming to stay for a couple of days, and I have to cook for them."},{"s":107.29,"e":114.33,"t":"Well, there are plenty of places to buy food in Kite Place – it’s the area by the harbour."},{"s":114.45,"e":117.78,"t":"Oh, OK, I’ll find that on the map."},{"s":118.28,"e":121.47,"t":"What sort of food do you need to get?"},{"s":121.56,"e":125.58,"t":"Well, neither of them eats meat but they both like fish."},{"s":125.76,"e":128.83,"t":"Well, there’s a really good fish market there."},{"s":128.97,"e":131.45,"t":"Oh great – where is it exactly?"},{"s":131.58,"e":139.13,"t":"It’s at the far end of Kite Place, so you have to go over the bridge and then it’s on the right."},{"s":139.39,"e":142.52,"t":"OK – is it open all day?"},{"s":142.8,"e":150.31,"t":"It doesn’t close until four, but I’d recommend going earlier than that – it does run out of some things."},{"s":150.32,"e":152.34,"t":"Oh, I don’t want that to happen."},{"s":152.57,"e":156.92,"t":"As long as you get there by 3.30, you should be fine."},{"s":157.2,"e":159.86,"t":"It’s only 11 now, so plenty of time."},{"s":160.79,"e":163.35,"t":"Do you need to buy vegetables too?"},{"s":163.48,"e":168.41,"t":"I do, and I want to avoid all the plastic packaging in the supermarket!"},{"s":168.47,"e":171.75,"t":"Well, there’s a really nice organic shop there."},{"s":172.15,"e":176.61,"t":"Now what’s it called … it’s the name of a flower."},{"s":176.89,"e":178.3,"t":"I know, it’s ‘Rose’."},{"s":178.36,"e":180.13,"t":"That’s a nice name."},{"s":180.09,"e":184.12,"t":"Yeah – it sells vegetables and quite a lot of other stuff."},{"s":184.11,"e":185.3,"t":"And where’s that?"},{"s":185.36,"e":193.29,"t":"Well, as you reach the market, you’ll see a big grey building on your left – I think it used to be a warehouse."},{"s":193.55,"e":203.14,"t":"Anyway, now it’s a restaurant upstairs, but the ground floor has two shops either side of the entrance and it’s the one on the left."},{"s":203.27,"e":204.44,"t":"That’s easy enough."},{"s":204.64,"e":211.23,"t":"You can’t miss it – there’s also a big sign on the pavement so you can look for that."},{"s":211.78,"e":217.68,"t":"I guess if I need anything else, I’ll have to go to the supermarket."},{"s":217.81,"e":225.55,"t":"Yeah – you should be able to get everything you need, but there’s a minibus that goes to the supermarket if you need it."},{"s":271.5,"e":274.95,"t":"The salmon is always very good and the shellfish."},{"s":275.01,"e":280.79,"t":"I’m going to make a curry, I think, and I need about 12 prawns for that."},{"s":280.85,"e":282.85,"t":"They’ll have plenty of those."},{"s":283.64,"e":286.12,"t":"Have you ever tried samphire?"},{"s":288,"e":290.19,"t":"It’s a type of seaweed."},{"s":290.34,"e":294.73,"t":"I just ask for a handful and you fry it in butter."},{"s":309.51,"e":312.95,"t":"Great – it’s always good to try something different."},{"s":313.53,"e":320.87,"t":"I’ll see what beans they have in the organic shop and I think I’ll get something for dessert there."},{"s":323.04,"e":326.74,"t":"I’m not sure – they’re not always ripe."},{"s":326.92,"e":330.14,"t":"I’d prefer a melon – it’s bigger too."},{"s":331.3,"e":339.63,"t":"The owner also sells a lot of spices there that you can put in a curry, and things like coconut."},{"s":339.6,"e":341.69,"t":"Oh, that’s very helpful."},{"s":341.66,"e":342.98,"t":"I’ll have a look."},{"s":344.19,"e":350.43,"t":"I know bread doesn’t really go with curry but I always like to have some in case."},{"s":350.43,"e":355.39,"t":"As I said – all the bread is home-made and there’s lots of variety."},{"s":355.77,"e":358.17,"t":"I like the brown bread myself."},{"s":366.06,"e":374.4,"t":"Well – not that, but they have a whole range of tarts and the best are the strawberry ones."},{"s":374.8,"e":379.05,"t":"Perfect – hopefully I won’t even have to go to the supermarket!"}],"2":[{"s":54.51,"e":62.68,"t":"The children’s book festival is coming up again soon and here to tell us all about it is the festival’s organiser, Jenny Morgan."},{"s":63,"e":65.88,"t":"So tell us what we can expect this year, Jenny."},{"s":66.21,"e":76.89,"t":"Well, as usual we’ve got five days of action-packed exciting events for children, with writers coming from all over the country getting involved."},{"s":77.24,"e":85.63,"t":"Just to give you an idea of what’s on offer in the workshops, first of all, there’s a very special event called Superheroes."},{"s":134.73,"e":143.08,"t":"This is a creative writing workshop encouraging children to describe situations where young people experience loneliness."},{"s":162.21,"e":166.4,"t":"It recently received the gold medal at the Waterford Awards."},{"s":185.78,"e":191.14,"t":"This will be a musical event where children will have the chance to play steel drums."},{"s":191.41,"e":196.88,"t":"This is bound to be very popular, so please book as soon as possible."},{"s":237.74,"e":243.12,"t":"I’m just wondering if you have a favourite book you could recommend for our readers?"},{"s":243.23,"e":248.82,"t":"It’s hard to choose, but Alive and Kicking is definitely worth mentioning."},{"s":249.1,"e":254.17,"t":"You won’t have heard of the writer as it’s her first book – which is really impressive."},{"s":254.44,"e":260.66,"t":"It’s basically the teenage diary of a boy from Somalia who comes to live in the UK."},{"s":260.7,"e":268.84,"t":"It deals with the serious issue of immigration and all the challenges the boy has to face at school and with the language barrier, etc."},{"s":269.08,"e":276.56,"t":"Usually, books like this are quite sad, but this one actually made me cry with laughter."},{"s":276.91,"e":283.46,"t":"On each page, there are simple but hilarious black and white stick drawings of the boy with his friends and teachers."},{"s":283.89,"e":292.07,"t":"At the end of each diary entry, there are new English words the boy learns each day, which may help develop some children’s vocabulary."},{"s":292.22,"e":294.76,"t":"I think my kids would enjoy that."},{"s":294.89,"e":300.53,"t":"What about any advice for parents on how to encourage their children to read more?"},{"s":300.64,"e":304.04,"t":"Well, this is something I get asked about a lot."},{"s":304.08,"e":309.92,"t":"There are so many distractions for kids these days that it can be hard to find time for reading."},{"s":310.41,"e":315.6,"t":"One thing I’d say is to make time to sit down with your child and share books with them."},{"s":315.6,"e":323.49,"t":"A lot of parents give up reading aloud to their children as soon as they learn to read independently, but this is a mistake."},{"s":323.61,"e":328.39,"t":"It’s good to read more advanced books to them as it helps to develop their vocabulary."},{"s":328.49,"e":333.54,"t":"If you don’t have time for this, then let them listen to audio books."},{"s":333.62,"e":337.2,"t":"Often, they’ll want to read books they’ve listened to for themselves."},{"s":348.38,"e":351.39,"t":"You can introduce new authors and genres to them."},{"s":351.42,"e":354.31,"t":"Librarians should be able to help you with this."}],"3":[{"s":68.95,"e":69.84,"t":"How about you?"},{"s":71.35,"e":74.62,"t":"I’m really struggling with my Year 12 science class."},{"s":74.69,"e":76.75,"t":"Are they hard to control?"},{"s":76.82,"e":79.73,"t":"Well, I don’t have discipline problems as such."},{"s":79.8,"e":84.41,"t":"It’s just that they don’t seem to think that science has anything to do with their lives."},{"s":85.43,"e":94.11,"t":"They listen to what I say, and I gave them a test last week and the results weren’t too bad, but there’s no real engagement."},{"s":94.59,"e":100.74,"t":"And as part of my teaching practice, I have to design an experiment for them to do."},{"s":100.72,"e":109.59,"t":"I was wondering about something on the children’s diets … you know, asking them to record what they eat and maybe linking it to their state of health."},{"s":110.77,"e":115.96,"t":"So your methodology would involve the children recording what they eat."},{"s":116.21,"e":126.45,"t":"OK, but you’d also need to have access to the children’s medical records and I don’t think people would be happy about that; confidentiality would be an issue."},{"s":127.23,"e":134.55,"t":"If you could get the right data, the conclusions might be significant, but I suspect it’s not going to be easy."},{"s":135.51,"e":138.75,"t":"Have you thought about doing an experiment using animals?"},{"s":138.8,"e":141.25,"t":"Wouldn’t that be upsetting for the children?"},{"s":141.37,"e":145.09,"t":"Well, the animals don’t have to be harmed in any way."},{"s":145.1,"e":150.95,"t":"It could just be an experiment where they’re given a certain diet and the effects are observed."},{"s":150.98,"e":154.1,"t":"Would I have to get permission to use animals?"},{"s":154.06,"e":161.76,"t":"Yes, you’d have to submit an outline of the experiment and fill in a form, but it’s quite straightforward."},{"s":161.7,"e":171.02,"t":"But if we found out that, say, a particular diet affects the health of animals, the same thing wouldn’t necessarily be true for people, would it?"},{"s":178.62,"e":183.14,"t":"So what animals could I use to investigate the effects of diet?"},{"s":185.19,"e":190.79,"t":"You’d need experimental mice – ones that have been specially bred for experiments."},{"s":191.09,"e":196.42,"t":"OK, so what will your experiment be investigating exactly?"},{"s":196.45,"e":199.24,"t":"Well, something to do with nutrition."},{"s":199.34,"e":206.67,"t":"So maybe we could look at food supplements … things like extra iron and extra protein, and their impact on health."},{"s":207.32,"e":210.1,"t":"That might be rather broad."},{"s":210.42,"e":215.91,"t":"Maybe just look at the effects of one supplement, like sugar, on the health of the mice?"},{"s":216.12,"e":221.59,"t":"In fact, maybe the focus could be on whether mice can control their own diet."},{"s":221.64,"e":226.19,"t":"So, what happens when they have access to more sugar, that they don’t really need?"},{"s":226.73,"e":230.39,"t":"Do they eat it or do they decide to leave it?"},{"s":231.51,"e":236.43,"t":"Then later on, you could do a follow-up experiment adding another variable."},{"s":236.68,"e":246.48,"t":"Like, you could give some of the mice the chance to be more active, running on a wheel or something, and the others just sit around and don’t do much."},{"s":246.49,"e":254.53,"t":"Or I could repeat the experiment but change the type of food I provided … or use mice with a different genetic structure."},{"s":309.71,"e":312.53,"t":"I did a similar experiment in college actually."},{"s":313.37,"e":315.57,"t":"So how many mice would I need?"},{"s":315.93,"e":317.81,"t":"I’d say about 12."},{"s":318.21,"e":321.91,"t":"And all young ones, not a mixture of old and young."},{"s":322.6,"e":328.9,"t":"And I’d need two groups of equal sizes, so six in each group."},{"s":329.23,"e":331.08,"t":"And how would I tell them apart?"},{"s":331.16,"e":337.6,"t":"I suppose I could put some sort of tag on one group … or just mark them in some way?"},{"s":337.52,"e":340.78,"t":"You could use food colouring, that wouldn’t hurt them."},{"s":341.29,"e":349.63,"t":"Then each group would go into a separate cage, and one group, let’s call them group A, would be the control group."},{"s":349.62,"e":352.3,"t":"So they’d just have ordinary mouse food."},{"s":352.49,"e":354.1,"t":"I suppose you can buy that?"},{"s":354.07,"e":356.17,"t":"Yes, it comes in dry pellets."},{"s":356.12,"e":361.68,"t":"And the other group would have the same as the first group, but they’d also have the extra sugar."},{"s":361.84,"e":363.96,"t":"Would you just give them straight sugar?"},{"s":364.13,"e":367.77,"t":"It might be better to give them something like cereal with it."},{"s":368.28,"e":372.21,"t":"Then you’d need to weigh the mice, I should think once a week."},{"s":372.63,"e":375.27,"t":"And you’d need an electronic balance."},{"s":375.24,"e":379.81,"t":"But we can’t hold them on the balance, or it’d affect the reading."},{"s":380.34,"e":385.51,"t":"So you need something called a weighing chamber to stop the mice from running away."},{"s":386.05,"e":391.92,"t":"It sounds complicated, but actually you can just use a plastic box with holes in the top."},{"s":392.34,"e":401.33,"t":"So once we’ve measured the weight gain of each mouse we can work out the average for each group, as well as the standard deviation."},{"s":401.56,"e":404.16,"t":"And then see where we go from there."},{"s":404.35,"e":408.37,"t":"That sounds cool, I think the students will enjoy it."}],"4":[{"s":72.22,"e":76.62,"t":"In today’s lecture, I’m going to be talking about microplastics."},{"s":77.4,"e":84.3,"t":"Microplastics are tiny pieces of plastic smaller than five millimetres in size."},{"s":85.05,"e":92.76,"t":"Recently there’s been a greater awareness that there are large quantities of plastic waste – big and small – in the environment."},{"s":93.69,"e":106.27,"t":"The amount of plastic waste in the oceans has received widespread attention, but far less is known about the effects of microplastics in freshwater and particularly in soil."},{"s":106.83,"e":112.97,"t":"Microplastics can enter the environment via a number of different sources."},{"s":113.27,"e":124.11,"t":"Threads and microfibres detach from synthetic clothing every time they’re put in a washing machine, and these find their way into the water system."},{"s":124.58,"e":135.95,"t":"Other sources include big pieces of plastic waste that are already in the environment, and these break down into microscopic particles over a period of time."},{"s":137.27,"e":148.13,"t":"On a larger scale, factory waste is another route, as are tyres which wear down as cars, lorries and so on travel along road surfaces."},{"s":149.67,"e":157.17,"t":"We already understand some of the impacts of microplastics from studies involving fish and other animals."},{"s":190.18,"e":197.63,"t":"What’s more, salt and many kinds of seafood have also been found to contain microplastics."},{"s":198.75,"e":207.21,"t":"However, it’s important to underline that there is not yet conclusive proof that microplastics cause significant harm to people."},{"s":208.18,"e":220.93,"t":"In many countries, including here in the UK, there is legislation which prevents manufacturers from adding plastic microbeads to shower gels, facial cleansers and toothpaste."},{"s":236.84,"e":248.48,"t":"What’s more, many of the fertilisers used by both farmers and gardeners contain microplastics."},{"s":249.65,"e":258.91,"t":"A team from the Anglia Ruskin University in Cambridge has carried out a study of the effects of microplastics on the digestive tracts of earthworms."},{"s":259.92,"e":266.73,"t":"These worms, which live in topsoil, are an essential component of our agricultural system."},{"s":267.71,"e":274.18,"t":"By feeding on soil, they mix nutrients into it, thereby making it more fertile."},{"s":274.47,"e":288.15,"t":"The researchers set out to discover whether the introduction of microplastics into the soil – and the subsequent ingestion of these by earthworms – would impact soil quality and ultimately inhibit plant growth."},{"s":288.28,"e":291.21,"t":"The short answer was, yes, it did."},{"s":299.47,"e":311.61,"t":"The particles of microplastic, which included biodegradable PLA and conventional high-density polyethylene, or HDPE, were then ingested by the earthworms in the soil."},{"s":312.09,"e":315.21,"t":"The result was that the worms lost weight rapidly."},{"s":330.5,"e":342.82,"t":"The team also discovered that there was an increase in the amount of acid found in the soil, and this was attributed mainly to the microplastic particles from conventional HDPE plastic."},{"s":344.14,"e":352.57,"t":"The conclusions of the study make for very interesting reading – I’ve included the reference in the notes to give you at the end of this session."},{"s":354.55,"e":361.74,"t":"To summarise, the authors proposed the idea that we need to regard soil as we would regard any other process in nature."},{"s":362.23,"e":371.49,"t":"This means we should accept the implications of soil being dependent on decaying and dead matter constantly being passed through the bodies of earthworms."},{"s":371.92,"e":382.71,"t":"That is, when soil becomes impoverished by the presence of microplastics, not only ecosystems but also the whole of society are negatively impacted."}]},"4":{"1":[{"s":94.79,"e":97.34,"t":"I’m Kaeden, one of the supervisors."},{"s":97.27,"e":98.64,"t":"Welcome to the team."},{"s":101.34,"e":102.84,"t":"I’m so sorry."},{"s":104.01,"e":108,"t":"People often get my name wrong; they never know how to spell it."},{"s":114.88,"e":116.29,"t":"I’ll try and remember."},{"s":116.44,"e":122.07,"t":"So, there are a few practical things you need to sort out this morning."},{"s":122.07,"e":124.53,"t":"Then I’ll show you what you’re going to do today."},{"s":138.15,"e":143.4,"t":"So, after you’ve finished at the front desk, I’ll take you to the staffroom."},{"s":143.44,"e":147.11,"t":"Put your coat and rucksack in one of the lockers there."},{"s":147.15,"e":148.68,"t":"Take whichever one is free."},{"s":148.84,"e":150.96,"t":"Will I have a key?"},{"s":151.65,"e":153.18,"t":"Try not to lose it."},{"s":153.57,"e":157.38,"t":"At the end of the day, leave it in the door for the next person to use."},{"s":158.7,"e":162.56,"t":"You also need to go to the HR department to see Tiffany."},{"s":162.56,"e":163.94,"t":"She’s really helpful."},{"s":164.26,"e":167.29,"t":"I was told to bring my passport with me."},{"s":167.37,"e":170.36,"t":"HR need to take a note of the number in it."},{"s":171.2,"e":173.14,"t":"Or you can show your ID card."},{"s":173.2,"e":175.32,"t":"I don’t have one of those."},{"s":175.79,"e":178.26,"t":"Tiffany will give you a uniform."},{"s":178.47,"e":182.1,"t":"They have lots in different sizes, so you just tell her what you need."},{"s":182.04,"e":186.61,"t":"I won’t come with you to HR – I’ve got to go and sort something else out."},{"s":187.01,"e":188.89,"t":"Problem with a bread slicer."},{"s":188.98,"e":191.61,"t":"Is the HR office near the staffroom?"},{"s":191.7,"e":198.08,"t":"The staffroom’s on the first floor, and HR are a couple of floors above that, on the third floor."},{"s":198.21,"e":200.65,"t":"There’s a staircase outside the staffroom."},{"s":201.21,"e":205.97,"t":"When you’ve finished with HR, come and find me in the bakery section of the shop."},{"s":206.11,"e":208.64,"t":"I’m looking forward to getting started."},{"s":274.38,"e":278.37,"t":"The first job is to check sell-by dates on the bread and cakes."},{"s":278.66,"e":282.83,"t":"If any of the dates are today’s, put a new price label on the packaging."},{"s":290.4,"e":293.69,"t":"Yes, but that shouldn’t happen – we check the stock every day."},{"s":294.08,"e":299.47,"t":"When something needs a new price label, put a yellow one on the package, next to the original price."},{"s":300.1,"e":303.81,"t":"After that, you’ll go to the sushi takeaway counter."},{"s":303.88,"e":307.51,"t":"Will I be preparing boxes of food?"},{"s":307.69,"e":310.12,"t":"For today, you’ll just be helping the staff."},{"s":310.22,"e":311.3,"t":"Yes, of course."},{"s":311.4,"e":315.29,"t":"You’ll see lots of flat cardboard boxes at one end of the counter."},{"s":315.63,"e":322.54,"t":"Beneath those is where we keep the plastic boxes – we run out of those really quickly, so you should bring more from the storeroom."},{"s":326.1,"e":330.57,"t":"You also need to clean the area where they prepare the dishes."},{"s":330.54,"e":333.35,"t":"There are cloths and bottles of spray by the sink."},{"s":333.46,"e":336.53,"t":"Oh, and please make sure you clean that too."},{"s":337.15,"e":339.19,"t":"That’s important, isn’t it?"},{"s":339.69,"e":341.98,"t":"But you mustn’t wash up knives."},{"s":342.08,"e":345.65,"t":"You have to do some training before you’re allowed to touch sharp objects."},{"s":345.87,"e":348.21,"t":"What should I do if there are any?"},{"s":348.3,"e":350.31,"t":"Ask someone to put them in the dishwasher."},{"s":351.93,"e":353.79,"t":"I don’t want to get anything wrong."},{"s":354.46,"e":355.33,"t":"You’ll be fine."},{"s":355.53,"e":356.87,"t":"And I’ll be around to help."},{"s":358.14,"e":360.67,"t":"Finally, the meat and fish counters."},{"s":360.53,"e":366.4,"t":"You need to clean the area where staff serve customers, including wiping the weighing scales."},{"s":369.17,"e":375.64,"t":"The fish is laid on ice, but when that starts to melt, you’ll need to get more from the cold-room."},{"s":375.68,"e":379.53,"t":"I know the staff on the food counters wear a hat."},{"s":379.66,"e":381.57,"t":"Will that be the same for me?"},{"s":381.79,"e":384.64,"t":"You won’t be serving customers directly, so no."},{"s":384.71,"e":388.91,"t":"But make sure you put on thermal gloves when you take anything out of the cold-room."},{"s":389.06,"e":392.86,"t":"The temperature’s low enough in there to get frostbite from touching things."}],"2":[{"s":49.85,"e":51.48,"t":"Welcome to my podcast."},{"s":51.82,"e":55.61,"t":"If you’re thinking about taking up running – I’m here to help."},{"s":55.7,"e":63.13,"t":"There are many training programmes available online which aim to help people build up to running 5 kilometres."},{"s":63.39,"e":72.87,"t":"Some of them are great and thousands of people of all ages are taking part in 5-kilometre races across the country as a result."},{"s":73.26,"e":78.84,"t":"People like them because they’re easy to follow and don’t push them too hard."},{"s":79.0,"e":90.47,"t":"However, they don’t work for everyone – especially if you suffer from something like a heart condition or asthma, because they’re aimed at people with average fitness and running ability."},{"s":90.73,"e":101.22,"t":"Another thing is that everyone is different – and if you have any specific questions related to your needs, there’s no one to provide any answers."},{"s":101.45,"e":106.7,"t":"I have a couple of simple tips I always give to new runners."},{"s":106.8,"e":115.89,"t":"I expect you’ve been told to run very slowly until your fitness increases – well, I find that can prevent progress."},{"s":116.21,"e":124.43,"t":"You should run at a speed that feels comfortable, but time yourself and try to run a bit faster each time."},{"s":124.57,"e":132.29,"t":"Listening to music can be very helpful – it takes your mind off things and helps your body get into a rhythm."},{"s":132.42,"e":141.66,"t":"I’d say that is better than running with a friend – especially as most people are competitive and that’s not what you want when you’re just starting."},{"s":215.76,"e":220.58,"t":"Ceri, for example, joined the club two years ago at the age of 40."},{"s":220.72,"e":226.17,"t":"She’d always enjoyed running at school but wasn’t sure if she’d be able to do it."},{"s":226.46,"e":230.86,"t":"She was worried about being left behind and being the slowest runner."},{"s":231.0,"e":237.22,"t":"But she says she was made to feel so welcome she soon forgot all about that."},{"s":237.64,"e":246.65,"t":"James had always hated the idea of running but a friend encouraged him to come along for a taster session and he hasn’t looked back."},{"s":246.76,"e":252.06,"t":"He never misses a training session despite having a really demanding job."},{"s":252.69,"e":263.39,"t":"Leo was worried about having to commit himself to training sessions every week and wasn’t sure he’d be able to fit training into his busy schedule."},{"s":263.6,"e":270.55,"t":"But after experiencing a lot of stress at work he came along to us and gave it a go."},{"s":270.57,"e":277.18,"t":"Now he says he feels much more relaxed and he looks forward to his weekly run."},{"s":277.45,"e":280.52,"t":"Mark is quite typical of our new members."},{"s":280.56,"e":290.5,"t":"He’s never considered himself to be a sporty person and it was only when he retired that he decided to take up the challenge of trying to run 5 kilometres."},{"s":290.6,"e":304.55,"t":"It took him months to find the courage to contact us but felt reassured immediately as there were other people his age who were only just taking up running for the first time."},{"s":304.79,"e":307.84,"t":"My own journey hasn’t been easy."},{"s":308.09,"e":313.42,"t":"I did my first marathon when I was 37, after having had two kids."},{"s":313.52,"e":320.25,"t":"My husband had been running marathons for years, but I never dreamed I’d be doing one with him."},{"s":320.42,"e":330.91,"t":"I managed to complete it in four hours, but I felt like giving up halfway through – it was only the support of the spectators that kept me going."},{"s":344.67,"e":353.13,"t":"I did my first 10K after only six months, which was certainly very challenging and not something I’d necessarily recommend."}],"3":[{"s":56.37,"e":60.87,"t":"So Jane – you’ll be off to Denmark soon to do your work placement."},{"s":60.92,"e":67.62,"t":"Yes, I’m really looking forward to it and I’ve just started packing up all my books to put in storage."},{"s":67.62,"e":69.88,"t":"Well, I hope they don’t get spoilt."},{"s":70.16,"e":75.86,"t":"It’s OK – my grandfather works in a bookshop and he told me how to pack them."},{"s":75.85,"e":77.07,"t":"Oh, that’s helpful."},{"s":77.34,"e":82.94,"t":"He says you have to support the spine otherwise the paper can come away from the cover."},{"s":83.02,"e":84.5,"t":"Yeah – that’s obvious."},{"s":98.95,"e":104.88,"t":"Well, it’s pretty clear that ruins them, but a lot of people just can’t be bothered to protect their books."},{"s":104.96,"e":110.02,"t":"He always says it’s such a shame that publishers don’t use better-quality paper."},{"s":110.1,"e":113.44,"t":"It’s the acid in the paper that causes the problem, isn’t it?"},{"s":113.45,"e":116.47,"t":"Yeah – that’s why old books go yellow."},{"s":116.54,"e":121.67,"t":"You know some of the books my grandfather’s given me are like that already."},{"s":122.11,"e":127.8,"t":"I should dump them really if they’re going to deteriorate further, but I’d feel bad."},{"s":127.97,"e":130.48,"t":"They’ll always remind me of him."},{"s":130.41,"e":132.51,"t":"He’s quite a collector, you know."},{"s":132.54,"e":134.38,"t":"Well, if they’re important to you …"},{"s":134.31,"e":137.46,"t":"Yeah – I’d regret just throwing them away."},{"s":137.58,"e":145.11,"t":"You know, maybe it’s because I was taught to treasure books … but I hate seeing students force open the pages – of paperbacks."},{"s":145.07,"e":148.12,"t":"They press so hard they end up breaking the spine."},{"s":148.31,"e":155.7,"t":"I know, but unfortunately, paperbacks aren’t designed to last a long time and people know that."},{"s":155.78,"e":157.61,"t":"Hardbacks aren’t quite as weak."},{"s":157.7,"e":160.17,"t":"Yeah, they’re different, I suppose."},{"s":160.46,"e":165.04,"t":"But I still don’t think people value hardbacks like they used to."},{"s":165.19,"e":169.06,"t":"Well, they aren’t decorative, are they, like other objects."},{"s":169.2,"e":174.64,"t":"Plus, nowadays, people don’t keep them out on shelves as much as they used to."},{"s":174.65,"e":176.04,"t":"That’s such a pity."},{"s":176.59,"e":183.7,"t":"When I visit someone – if they have, say, a colourful book on a table, it’s the first thing I’m drawn to."},{"s":190.43,"e":193.86,"t":"I’ve always been taught to handle books carefully."},{"s":194.13,"e":198.57,"t":"If you watch someone take a book off a shelf, well, they usually do it wrong."},{"s":212.18,"e":213.85,"t":"When did you learn all this?"},{"s":213.87,"e":221.06,"t":"He watched me pull a heavy book off the shelf when I was small, and it fell on the floor and broke apart."},{"s":222.13,"e":224.26,"t":"I can still remember it!"},{"s":224.42,"e":226.27,"t":"You know what I really like?"},{"s":226.74,"e":228.69,"t":"The smell of new books."},{"s":229.77,"e":234.54,"t":"My parents used to laugh at me when I was a kid because I loved putting books up to my nose."},{"s":234.54,"e":236.24,"t":"Almost as much as reading them!"},{"s":236.33,"e":238.93,"t":"New books aren’t cheap, though, are they?"},{"s":239.01,"e":240.8,"t":"I guess we’re lucky we can buy them."},{"s":293.72,"e":294.9,"t":"What’s it like?"},{"s":295.05,"e":303.44,"t":"Well, it’s quite big – it’s got two floors and an attic, and he stocks all kinds of books really."},{"s":303.59,"e":307.54,"t":"I guess he treasures things like first editions and other rare books."},{"s":307.61,"e":312.0,"t":"Yeah – you might think he’d keep those in the attic or somewhere."},{"s":312.07,"e":313.64,"t":"… so they’d be hidden?"},{"s":323.41,"e":325.09,"t":"That would prevent any thefts!"},{"s":325.89,"e":327.7,"t":"Does he stock books for children?"},{"s":328.69,"e":339.05,"t":"He particularly likes to encourage kids to read; he always says that he used to sit under the stairs as a child with a pile of books and read them all."},{"s":339.45,"e":341.08,"t":"Is that where he keeps them, then?"},{"s":341.03,"e":352.6,"t":"Not exactly – he’s got a dedicated area on the ground floor with cushions so that parents can enter with their toddlers, go there and spend some time reading to them."},{"s":353.96,"e":357.43,"t":"And then there’s a place for pushchairs by the front door."},{"s":357.43,"e":360.49,"t":"And a café if anyone needs refreshments."},{"s":360.42,"e":361.47,"t":"That’s good to know."},{"s":361.5,"e":367.12,"t":"As I said, it’s a big shop and there’s a storage area out the back as well."},{"s":367.15,"e":369.32,"t":"Oh, what does he keep there?"},{"s":369.31,"e":370.91,"t":"Books he wants to throw away?"},{"s":370.94,"e":378.28,"t":"He hardly ever throws anything away – he just leaves unwanted books by the front door for customers to take."},{"s":378.35,"e":380.28,"t":"Well, that’s very nice."},{"s":380.14,"e":387.17,"t":"Yeah – and books people or institutions have requested, they all go at the far end."},{"s":387.71,"e":393.56,"t":"He thinks it’s best to keep these out of the main shopping area as they’re boxed and new."},{"s":393.72,"e":395.76,"t":"Did you get your coursebooks from him?"},{"s":396.27,"e":399.42,"t":"He stocks books for a lot of the colleges."},{"s":399.47,"e":409.6,"t":"He used to keep these books on the first floor, but now there’s a new university in my hometown, he’s moved them downstairs to attract the students."},{"s":409.65,"e":414.23,"t":"They’re actually part of the coffee shop, on low shelves all around it."},{"s":414.28,"e":415.69,"t":"Pretty central then."}],"4":[{"s":85.98,"e":91.41,"t":"But unfortunately, tree planting isn’t as straightforward as some people think."},{"s":91.96,"e":102.34,"t":"When the wrong trees are planted in the wrong place, it can do considerably more damage than good, failing to help either people or the environment."},{"s":103.25,"e":113.5,"t":"Reforestation projects are currently being undertaken on a huge scale in many countries and it’s crucial that the right trees are selected."},{"s":114.14,"e":127.44,"t":"A mix of species should always be planted, typical of the local natural forest ecosystem and including rare and endangered species in order to create a rich ecosystem."},{"s":127.82,"e":133.34,"t":"It’s important to avoid non-native species that could become invasive."},{"s":134.01,"e":148.44,"t":"Invasive species are a significant contributor to the current global biodiversity crisis and are often in competition with native species and may threaten their long-term survival."},{"s":149.82,"e":163.58,"t":"Restoring biodiversity that will maximise carbon capture is key when reforesting an area, but ideally any reforestation project should have several goals."},{"s":164.14,"e":177.45,"t":"These could include selecting trees that can contribute to wildlife conservation, improve the availability of food for the local community and maintain the stability of soil systems."},{"s":178.22,"e":193.22,"t":"Meeting as many of these goals as possible, whilst doing no harm to local communities, native ecosystems and vulnerable species, is the sign of a highly successful tree-planting scheme."},{"s":194.23,"e":211.39,"t":"To ensure the survival and resilience of a planted forest, it’s vital to use tree seeds with appropriate levels of genetic diversity: the amount of genetic variation found within a species essential for their survival."},{"s":212.23,"e":226.35,"t":"Using seeds with low genetic diversity generally lowers the resilience of restored forests, which can make them vulnerable to disease and unable to adapt to climate change."},{"s":227.64,"e":235.14,"t":"Choosing the right location for reforestation projects is as important as choosing the right trees."},{"s":235.86,"e":244.77,"t":"Ultimately, the best area for planting trees would be in formerly forested areas that are in poor condition."},{"s":245.27,"e":259.13,"t":"It’s better to avoid non-forested landscapes such as natural grasslands, savannas or wetlands as these ecosystems already contribute greatly to capturing carbon."},{"s":259.92,"e":268.98,"t":"It would also be advantageous to choose an area where trees could provide other benefits, such as recreational spaces."},{"s":269.57,"e":281.79,"t":"Reforesting areas which are currently exploited for agriculture should be avoided as this often leads to other areas being deforested."},{"s":283.8,"e":290.26,"t":"Large-scale reforestation projects require careful planning."},{"s":290.85,"e":297.6,"t":"Making the right decisions about where to plant trees depends on having the right information."},{"s":298.04,"e":307.2,"t":"Having detailed and up-to-date maps identifying high-priority areas for intervention is essential."},{"s":308.01,"e":317.64,"t":"Drone technology is a useful tool in helping to prioritise and monitor areas of degraded forest for restoration."},{"s":318.18,"e":332.37,"t":"In Brazil, it’s being used to identify and quantify how parts of the Amazon are being devastated by human activities such as rearing cattle and illegal logging."},{"s":333.75,"e":342.66,"t":"A good example of where the right trees were picked to achieve a restored forest is in Lampang Province in Northern Thailand."},{"s":342.83,"e":354.87,"t":"A previously forested site which had been degraded through mining was reforested by a cement company together with Chiang Mai University."},{"s":355.25,"e":367.29,"t":"After spreading 60 cm of topsoil, they planted 14 different native tree species which included several species of fig."},{"s":367.8,"e":376.05,"t":"Figs are a keystone species because of the critical role they play in maintaining wildlife populations."},{"s":376.27,"e":391.17,"t":"They are central to tropical reforestation projects as they accelerate the speed of the recovery process by attracting animals and birds which act as natural seed dispersers."},{"s":391.71,"e":398.85,"t":"This helps to promote diversity through the healthy regrowth of a wide range of plant species."},{"s":399.41,"e":409.38,"t":"Unlike the majority of fruit trees, figs bear fruit all year round, providing a reliable food source for many species."},{"s":409.54,"e":423.22,"t":"At this site, for example, after only three rainy seasons, monkeys started visiting to eat the fig fruits, naturally dispersing seeds through defecation."},{"s":423.59,"e":433.52,"t":"Reforestation projects should always aim to make sure that local communities are consulted and involved in the decision-making process."},{"s":434.2,"e":444.19,"t":"The restoration of mangrove forests in Madagascar is an example of a project which has succeeded in creating real benefits for the community."},{"s":445.3,"e":461.23,"t":"Destruction of the mangrove forests had a terrible impact on plant and animal life, and also badly affected the fishing industry, which was a major source of employment for local people living in coastal areas."},{"s":461.7,"e":470.66,"t":"The reforestation project involved hiring local people to plant and care for the new mangrove trees."},{"s":471.39,"e":479.47,"t":"Millions of mangrove trees have now been planted which has resulted in the return of a healthy aquatic ecosystem."},{"s":479.78,"e":488.05,"t":"The mangroves also act as a defence against the increased threat of flooding caused by climate change."},{"s":488.47,"e":498.49,"t":"What’s more, the local economy is more stable and thousands more Madagascans are now able to send their children to school."}]},"ext":"mp3"};
